Decision Engines
Signal Enhancement: Strategy Intelligence API applies AI scoring to raw signals before risk gate. Model providers: OpenAI (primary), Gemini (secondary), Groq (free fallback).

Scoring Model: Walk-forward ranker (client/src/lib/replayWalkForwardRanker.ts) uses historical replay data to score strategies. strategyScoringEngine.ts applies expectancy-weighted ranking.

Learning Systems
Walk-Forward Validation: engine/cmd/sep_evidence/ + client/src/app/api/sep/ implements the Strategy Evidence Program — systematic out-of-sample validation for each strategy before promotion to live capital.

WINNERS_ONLY Gate: Active since May 2026. Any strategy with negative expectancy (after fees) is automatically removed from the registry. Fee model updated to match actual broker costs.

AI Risks
API dependency risk: OpenAI/Gemini/Groq outages degrade AI scoring. Fallback chain exists but degrades gracefully only to Groq free tier.
Stub packages: engine/internal/ml/ and engine/internal/research_ai/ are empty — planned but not implemented.
No model versioning: No MLflow or model registry. Models called via API only — version control is external.
Prompt injection risk: AI receives market text data; no sanitization layer documented.
Latency risk: AI scoring adds round-trip latency to signal path. Not suitable for sub-100ms execution.
